Subject: [PATCH 11316/11362] Correct two surface-scan figures by parsing: 46
 to 33 empty-flag assertions, 88 to 89 KeyErrors

Both figures in the substrate-class note were carried from a text scan while the
parsed count disagreed, the pattern three reviews found today.

- "46 empty-flag assertions" was a grep count; its pattern also matched `n_warn`
  shapes and validators' own `flags` lists. By AST parse: 33 assertions of the form
  `assert <x>["flags"] == []` in 31 files; 5 call the verifier in the test body, 9
  assert a capstone's stored `adversarial_verify_report`. The conclusion stands on the
  measured probe (a universal warn broke an existing test on a real artifact) and on
  the 9, not on the 46.
- "88 KeyError failures in seven archive tests" was a hand tally that dropped the one
  failure in the exp3722 convergence-synthesis test. Direct line counts over the saved
  pytest output: 131 FAILED lines, 89 KeyError lines, 89 FAILED lines across those
  seven files, 10 in exp6780.
- The script written to re-derive the second figure by splitting the pytest output
  into sections found 49 sections for 131 failures and was discarded; the direct
  line counts were used. Recorded in the note, section 9.

The same wording lives in the docstring of check_substrate_class and in the
SCENARIO-2 test comment; those two files follow in the next commit after merging
main, whose eval-run lint fix removes the need for any runs-directory symlink.

